<Base title="About & installation">
  <p class="back-link"><a href="/">Back to the gallery</a></p>
  <header class="page-heading"><h1>Know your<br /><span>download.</span></h1><p class="intro">A small, curated archive of community PNGs for Tesla Paint Shop's vehicle visualization.</p></header>
  <div class="about-layout">
    <nav class="page-nav" aria-label="About this page"><a href="#archive">The archive</a><a href="#sources">Sources &amp; licences</a><a href="#templates">Official templates</a><a href="#validation">What we check</a><a href="#installation">Installation</a></nav>
    <div class="prose">
      <section id="archive"><p class="micro-label">01 / The archive</p><h2>Made for the screen</h2><p>These images change the vehicle visualization in Paint Shop. They are digital designs for the screen, not files for a physical vinyl wrap.</p><p>We curate the catalogue. This version has no user uploads. The gallery may include candidate designs awaiting rights review. Each thumbnail is a flat PNG preview rather than a 3D vehicle render.</p></section>
      <section id="sources"><p class="micro-label">02 / Sources &amp; licences</p><h2>Follow the source</h2><p>We accept original work from its creator and third-party work released under CC0. Each design page records its author, licence and provenance. Third-party records also include the source, licence evidence and retrieval date.</p><p>Original work may use <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>, which requires attribution, or <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/">CC0 1.0</a>, a public-domain dedication. Candidate designs are awaiting rights review; their proposed CC0 designation does not grant reuse rights. Read the licence on the design page before reusing any other file. A gallery listing does not grant rights to unrelated logos or trademarks.</p></section>
      <section id="templates"><p class="micro-label">03 / Official templates</p><h2>The right shape for your model</h2><p>Each vehicle page links to its folder in <a href="https://github.com/teslamotors/custom-wraps">Tesla's official custom-wraps repository</a>. We link to those templates and examples rather than copy them into this archive. Their presence in Tesla's repository is not a licence for us to redistribute them.</p></section>
      <section id="validation"><p class="micro-label">04 / File validation</p><h2>A checked file is a starting point</h2><p>Our build checks PNG properties, vehicle-template dimensions, filenames, file size and the required licence and source records. Downloads preserve the original PNG bytes.</p><p>These checks do not prove that Tesla's app or a vehicle will accept a file, or that the design aligns correctly on the 3D model. The gallery does not claim in-car verification. Check your model, software and the current official instructions before installing.</p></section>
      <section id="installation"><p class="micro-label">05 / Installation</p><h2>Take it to Paint Shop</h2><p>Choose the PNG for your exact vehicle variant. Tesla documents two transfer methods in its <a href="https://github.com/teslamotors/custom-wraps#how-to-use-custom-wraps">official installation guide</a>.</p><h3>With the mobile app</h3><ol><li>Download the original PNG to your phone.</li><li>Use Tesla app version 4.59.0 or later. Open <strong>Creations &gt; Wrap &gt; Upload</strong> and select the PNG.</li><li>In the vehicle, open <strong>Toybox &gt; Paint Shop &gt; Wraps</strong> and apply the design.</li></ol><h3>With a USB drive</h3><ol><li>Use a drive formatted as exFAT, FAT32 on Windows, MS-DOS FAT on Mac, ext3 or ext4. Tesla does not support NTFS for this use.</li><li>Create a folder named <code>Wraps</code> at the root of the drive and put the PNG inside it. Keep map and firmware update files off this drive.</li><li>Connect the drive to the vehicle, then open <strong>Toybox &gt; Paint Shop &gt; Wraps</strong>.</li></ol><p>Tesla allows up to 10 wraps from the app and up to 10 from USB. The official repository is the source for current requirements and troubleshooting.</p></section>
    </div>
  </div>
